OL,3,GNEWSAMad cow disease case confirmed at
OL,4,Afarm in Dumfries and Galloway
OL,5,
OL,6,FA case of Bovine Spongiform
OL,7,FEncephalopathy (BSE) has been confirmed
OL,8,Fin a cow on a farm in Dumfries and
OL,9,FGalloway.
OL,11,FThe infection, often called mad cow
OL,12,Fdisease, was identified as a result of
OL,13,Froutine testing and is an isolated
OL,14,Fcase.
OL,16,FThe animal did not enter the human food
OL,17,Fchain and Food Standards Scotland said
OL,18,Fthere was no risk to human health.
OL,20,FIt is the first case of classical BSE
OL,21,Fto be reported in Scotland since 2024.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
